  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Border Management Capacities in Armenia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the Project is to further strengthen the capacities of the Armenian Border Guard Troops (BGT) to tackle security and migration management challenges in line with international obligations, standards, and border management best practices. The Project will build on results achieved in recent years, specifically in the alignment of the BGT training and educational system and standards with European and international best practices and will further strengthen the capacity of the troops in this regard through delivery of trainings on contemporary adult learning techniques and adjusting the eLearning Solution (MOODLE system) of the BGT Training Centre. Moreover, recently, BGT have set up the secondary inspection/ interview line at selected border crossing points. Trainings on contemporary methods of document protection and fraud detection, as well as document examination and passenger profiling techniques were delivered to BGT specialists.  The Project will provide further support to the BGT in strengthening the capacity for secondary line inspections through additional document examination training, cross-border networking and learning activities and provision of the modern document examination equipment.</narrative>
  </description>
